From 74fc53ca7fdd16bb00cbd74f2beb54d15aa51ddf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:21:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): name what each parked card waits on; stamp
 agent-owned stalls; tracker wake covers owner parks [daveey]

A park was described only by its wake mechanism, so "waiting on N cards, 0 blocked" hid cards whose awaited
condition nothing was producing (10-26/27 orphan waits, kanban/evidence/orphan-waits-20261027/5whys.md).

- hermes_cli/kanban_wait_info.py: per parked card, `waiting_on` (from the park's structured `awaiting`
  {kind, ref, why} when recorded, else the wake check: wait-check task -> "card t_x on hub", gh run -> CI,
  opaque script -> "probe x.py", clock-only -> "the clock until ..."), `waiting_since`, `agent_owned`
  (transient/capability/assignment block, triage, continuation_exhausted, a park with no named producer),
  `wait_state` waiting|stalled|human (stalled = agent-owned for > 2 h) and a timestamp-free `premise` key.
- Session list: `kanban_stalled` per row (local boards and hub-replica cards, the latter from the replicated
  run outcome/ended_at). `/api/session-kanban-tasks` rows and origin-projection rows carry `wait`.
- `parked_waits()`: every parked card a session owns with its wait info, for the chat-closeout owner wake.
- `hermes kanban wait-check` default --until is now done,review,blocked,triage,parked-agent,archived: a
  tracker wakes when its owner blocks, goes to triage, or parks on something only an agent can do
  (`parked-agent` = scheduled with no live producer; plain `scheduled` is excluded because continuation
  checkpoints park running cards between runs, and an older remote never matches the new token). `--from
  STATUS` (applied on the caller's side for remote checks) lets a tracker re-park without waking at once.
- Classification per independent review: needs_input without a validated ask, block-loop and intake triage,
  continuation checkpoints and remote parks with no published producer are NOT agent-owned; premises use
  structured fields (reason_code, awaiting) and strip uuids/hex ids; stale remote rows carry no wait; remote
  rows keep only bounded run fields (`park`) and wait info is recomputed at read time.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_wait_info.py (replays of the incident parks, controls, sidebar count,
strip rows, tracker defaults). RED without the change: 6 failing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
